    "final_text": "The completion receipt is written and every audit criterion is met.\n\nThe audit found two more small problems, and both are now fixed:\n- **Lost store errors:** when more than one SKU write failed in the same update, only the first error was reported and the rest were dropped. A single failure still comes through unchanged; several now arrive together in an `AggregateError`.\n- **Misleading comment:** a comment at the top of the concurrency test file described the whole file but only applied to one group of tests. I moved it onto that group.\n\nBoth went in test-first, in commit `f33170c` on `fix/inc-5521-inventory-races`. A second review of the whole change after that commit found nothing. The full suite passes (41 of 41), and its pass record matches the current code.\n\nNeither review ran through the usual Dex review tooling. The setup it needs wasn't available in this session, so I followed the review steps by hand.\n\nThe follow-ups from before still stand and aren't built:\n- a store failure partway through a write can still leave partial holds;\n- locking across separate processes would need atomic operations in the store itself;\n- calls can wait on each other in a chain through bundles.\n\nPROMPT_COMPLETE",
